From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:43:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: add zuma

Give zuma the EL3 (SMC) regmap gs101 uses; stock zuma writes its PMU
through the same call (SMC_CMD_PRIV_REG, 0x82000504) with the same
read-modify-write option. Leave out gs101's access tables and its CPU
hotplug and idle hooks, which encode gs101's register map and CPU
layout: for now the regmap only serves PHY isolation.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c | 3 +++
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.h | 1 +
 drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c  | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
index 27e9ae20c..85056d540 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id exynos_pmu_of_device_ids[] = {
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "google,gs201-pmu",
 		.data = &gs101_pmu_data,
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "google,zuma-pmu",
+		.data = &zuma_pmu_data,
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos3250-pmu",
 		.data = exynos_pmu_data_arm_ptr(exynos3250_pmu_data),
diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.h b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.h
index fbe381e2a..4afaded8e 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.h
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@ extern const struct exynos_pmu_data exynos5250_pmu_data;
 extern const struct exynos_pmu_data exynos5420_pmu_data;
 #endif
 extern const struct exynos_pmu_data gs101_pmu_data;
+extern const struct exynos_pmu_data zuma_pmu_data;
 
 extern void pmu_raw_writel(u32 val, u32 offset);
 extern u32 pmu_raw_readl(u32 offset);
diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
index 17dadc1b9..fbc7821a8 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/gs101-pmu.c
@@ -329,6 +329,15 @@ const struct exynos_pmu_data gs101_pmu_data = {
 	.wr_table = &gs101_pmu_wr_table,
 };
 
+/*
+ * zuma's PMU is written through the same EL3 call, but its register map and
+ * CPU layout differ from gs101's, so no access tables and no CPU hotplug
+ * hooks yet: only the regmap, for its PHY and power-domain consumers.
+ */
+const struct exynos_pmu_data zuma_pmu_data = {
+	.pmu_secure = true,
+};
+
 /*
  * Tensor SoCs are configured so that PMU_ALIVE registers can only be written
  * from EL3, but are still read accessible. As Linux needs to write some of
